WEBVTT

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:04.730
<i>We only had a short time together.</i>

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.740
<i>But I enjoyed it.</i>

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:13.320
<i>I believe in Zakuro-san,
I’m sure she’ll come back!</i>

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:25.800
Oneesama?

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:38.100
We’re having a private conversation,
so stop bothering us.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.390
Quiche, what on earth are you talking about?

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:42.810
Zakuro-san is our...

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:44.770
...ally, you wanna say?

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.310
I was watching your last fight.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:55.320
If you really are allies, why didn’t
she transform and fight...

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.870
when your precious friend was having so
much trouble, just trying to help her?

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:00.160
So, why?

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.240
That’s...

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.890
Stop talking nonsense!

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:05.870
Oneesama, say something too!

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:07.710
Oneesama!?

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:09.010
Zakuro-san!

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:14.630
I’ve known for a while how strong
you are. If you were to join me,

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:16.840
I’d forget everything you’ve done to me so far.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:18.720
Quiche, it’s enou...!

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.010
Ichigo, you stay quiet!

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:23.480
<i>I’m sorry, it seems I’ve made a mistake.</i>

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.640
I just found the source of the signal for the Mew Aqua!

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:28.150
It’s not a ship!

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:29.610
The Mew Aqua is there!

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:32.860
What? How can it be there?

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:35.820
I rechecked the footage from the fight and...

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:42.290
That Zakuro... Had she realized it?

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:45.120
Ichigo, what are you upset about?

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.250
Only one of your teammates
is leaving you.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.210
Are you feeling insecure?

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:53.370
Well, no matter how hard you try to protect the Earth,

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:55.970
there’s no way you could possibly stand up to Deep Blue.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:57.830
Deep Blue...

00:01:57.830 --> 00:02:00.760
You’ve mentioned him before.
What is he?

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.060
He is the god who sent us here.

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:07.150
I’m telling you this because he has
nothing to do with me anymore.

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:12.400
Deep Blue is planning his awakening
with the help of the Mew Aqua.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:13.610
What?

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:18.160
And an awakened god is invincible!

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:21.280
Ah, wait!

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.280
Oneesama!

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:27.910
See ya.

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:29.170
Wait a minute.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.500
Why are you doing this?

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:36.210
I told you, didn’t I? The reason why
we’re looking for the Mew Aqua?

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:39.680
I doubt that is your <i>current</i> goal.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:44.550
I don’t know why you approached me,

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.270
but I was serious when I asked you to lend me a hand.

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:50.940
What are you trying to do... alone?

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:57.280
I have... something I need to do.

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:01.820
Hello, this is Retasu.

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:03.240
<i>It’s me, Shirogane.</i>

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:05.910
<i>We’ve located the Mew Aqua.</i>

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:07.290
<i>Get over there quickly.</i>

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:09.250
<i>We’ll wait for you there.</i>

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:10.790
Ichigo-san.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:15.540
If what Quiche said is true, we can’t
let them have the Mew Aqua!

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.000
Let’s hurry!

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:32.640
Is it here?

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:35.310
This place is a protective area for wild birds, right?

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:36.610
Ah, there they are!

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:38.650
You’re late?

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:39.570
Everyone.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:43.610
Shirogane. Is it really here?

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:46.160
I checked the video, and...

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:48.710
...confirmed that one of the migratory birds from the north...

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:51.790
...was holding the Mew Aqua, as if it were its treasure.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:53.580
It’s true!

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:54.920
I never would have guessed...

00:03:56.250 --> 00:04:00.130
The swan should be somewhere
in this protective area now.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:04.510
Uhm... why did the swan bring the
Mew Aqua all the way here?

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.510
Well, we don’t know the reason.

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:10.230
Anyway, we need to find that swan now.

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:16.560
But birds are cautious. As soon as they
feel someone coming, they will flee...

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.570
We have no other choice than
to trick them and catch them!

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.160
Poor birds.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:23.780
Calm down!

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:26.200
What are you trying to say?

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:31.580
What’s going on...?

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.500
They’re gathering all of a sudden!

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:36.840
But... that’s...

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:43.260
You guys... that’s why you brought the Mew Aqua?

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:52.930
I know! Minto-san can talk with birds!

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:55.020
Just like you, Ichigo, can talk with cats.

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:56.150
I see!

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:58.360
But I...

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:08.870
That’s...?!

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:21.170
...the Mew Aqua!

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:30.230
Hmm!

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:31.390
They’re coming!

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:35.060
Give us the Mew Aqua!

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:36.430
Let’s go!

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:41.280
Mew Mew Strawberry METAMORPHO-SE!

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:54.560
Mew Mew Lettuce METAMORPHO-SE!

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:04.640
Mew Mew Pudding METAMORPHO-SE!

00:06:20.390 --> 00:06:21.310
Minto-san!

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:22.570
Minto, what are you doing?

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:25.410
Fuu Rai Sen!

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:27.450
StrawberBell!

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:29.240
Tart!

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:30.570
Ok!

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:33.290
Minto! Hurry!

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:36.290
Ahh, that thing again!

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:38.830
Reborn Lettuce Rush!

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:46.750
Reborn PuddingRings Inferno!

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:48.510
Wait, Taru-taru!

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:49.590
Youuuu!

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:52.050
Minto! Hurry and transform!

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:53.260
I can’t.

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:57.170
Oneesama betrayed us.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:02.940
Take that, that, and that!

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:04.730
You, let me go, argh!

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:05.650
No way!

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:08.280
This is the end of the Mew Project.

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:09.780
I...

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:20.200
What is it doing?

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:23.880
It’s saving us a lot of effort and
bringing us the Mew Aqua.

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:26.540
But... I don’t think I can...

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:28.840
No! Please don’t ask me!

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.970
No!  NOO!

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:46.280
Ah, wait!

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:49.320
Annoying birds!

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:53.070
Darn it!

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:55.540
Wait, the signal is gone.

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:58.740
We can’t find it among
so many birds.

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:00.650
We have to come up with
a new plan first.

00:08:00.650 --> 00:08:01.540
Tsk.

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:07.180
Why... How could the Mew Aqua disappear?

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:10.710
Minto!

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:15.310
I couldn’t get over the fact that Oneesama betrayed us.

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:18.900
I know... this isn’t the right attitude.

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:23.480
The birds were crying desperately, “Help us!”

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:31.400
They showed me their feelings of
pain, anger, sadness, and desire.

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:37.120
Their instincts told them that the light of the Mew Aqua would save them,

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:38.790
so they brought it here.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:43.080
Yet... I refused them!

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:47.300
I refused them, who have brought us
the Mew Aqua in their desperation!

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:53.010
I didn’t realize Oneesama was so important to me.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:54.470
Minto-san...

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:56.220
Minto-oneechan.

00:08:57.110 --> 00:08:59.030
I still believe...

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:01.720
that Zakuro didn’t betray us.

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:03.430
So...

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:06.150
Ichigo, people change, and so do their hearts.

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:10.240
We have to grow much stronger.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:19.240
No chance, the signal is totally gone.

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:24.260
Just... why did the Mew Aqua stop shining all of a sudden?

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:29.210
As if its power had moved into something else...

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:32.170
Perhaps you are right.

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:36.680
The power of the Mew Aqua can
be stored in anything, so...

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:39.140
How troublesome...

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:43.600
Ryou, what do you think about Minto’s words?

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:46.610
That Zakuro is a traitor?

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:52.270
If so, it means I’m not qualified to be a leader.

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:53.950
That’s all.

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:11.580
Hey, Masha, what does that mean?

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:16.010
Why did Zakuro-san...?

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:17.170
<i>Enough!</i>

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:19.470
<i>We’ve gone through a lot of fights,</i>

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:23.480
<i>but you still don’t understand what it means to save the Earth, do you?</i>

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:25.980
Why all of sudden...?

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:28.350
<i>Honestly, I’ve run out of patience.</i>

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:31.900
<i>I haven’t decided yet what to do about that job,</i>

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:38.200
<i>but that doesn’t mean that the possibility of going is zero.</i>

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:39.490
<i>Ichigo,</i>

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:40.660
<i>Yes?</i>

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:43.120
<i>take care of Minto please.</i>

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:46.670
<i>Zakuro-san?</i>

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:54.550
After all, she is trying to provoke us, to
make us realize we have to be more reliable.

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:58.420
But, even then, why...?

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:06.430
Masha!

00:11:07.450 --> 00:11:11.390
Taa taa taa, it’s time for Bu-Ling’s fortune telling!

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:14.770
You’re not very happy right now, are you, Minto-oneechan?

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:19.860
So then, I’ll tell your fortune! How well do
you get along with Zakuro-oneechan?

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:22.820
Now, I will push this button!

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:26.700
What’s the result? This is exciting.

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:27.790
Uh-oh.

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:32.420
This answer can’t be right.
It does this sometimes.

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:34.250
Let’s try again!

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:36.750
Hmm, hmm...

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:39.260
Huh, Minto-oneechan?

00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:41.900
I’m going out for a while.

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:45.810
Come back safely...

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:48.930
Huh, where’s Minto?

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:51.520
She’s left. Geez.

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:53.440
I wonder where she went.

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:55.900
What’s up?

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:56.980
Shirogane.

00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:59.260
Oh, yes!!! Now for our next
fortune telling.

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:03.450
How well does Retasu-oneechan get along with Shirogane-oniichan?

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:04.870
<i>Oh, Bu-Ling-san, p-p-please don’t!</i>

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:08.530
<i>Why not? Wouldn’t you want to know if you
and Shirogane-oniichan make a nice..</i>

00:12:08.530 --> 00:12:09.830
<i>Nooooo!!!</i>

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:11.200
Hey, Shirogane.

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:14.960
<i>I TOLD you to keep that a secret
no matter what didn’t I?</i>

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:12.330
What is it?

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:14.080
I’ve been thinking.

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:20.050
Zakuro-san did that on purpose so we
could become more independent.

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:19.090
<i>Ah, he doesn’t know?  Why is it a secret?</i>

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:21.720
<i>Just keep it secret, ple-eease!</i>

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:21.720
Am I right?

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:23.170
Ah, well...

00:12:23.170 --> 00:12:27.720
I am sure that you know her true feelings, Shirogane!

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:31.560
Uhm, kind of.

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:32.730
She said:

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:36.600
<i>Let me say just one thing.</i>

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:39.180
<i>We are little girls.</i>

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:44.940
<i>Even though as Mew Mews we have always
been fighting, we are not “real warriors”.</i>

00:12:44.940 --> 00:12:48.910
<i>However, in the future, when the enemy’s
attacks become more severe,</i>

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:54.080
<i>each of us must be a strong warrior with faith in ourselves in order to protect the Earth.</i>

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:57.580
I was right after all.

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:00.210
So that’s how it is.

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:03.510
But, then why is she with Quiche now?

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:06.800
Well, that I don’t know.

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:07.720
Everyone!

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.430
What’s wrong, Keiichirou?

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:15.140
I just caught a signal at the wild bird area...
Minto-san and Zakuro-san transformed!

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:17.020
Did the aliens appear?

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:20.280
No, no sign of them!

00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:23.320
No way... Does that mean they’re fighting each other?

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:26.320
Let’s go, Retasu, Bu-Ling!
We have to stop them!

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:26.950
Yes.

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:27.950
We have to.

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:36.800
You were sulky and didn’t fight them, and now you’re regretting it.

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:38.210
That’s what your face looks like.

00:13:38.890 --> 00:13:44.710
Yes, that’s right, and I regret that I believed in you.

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:45.920
“Believed”?

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:49.620
If you had believed in me, you wouldn’t have been disturbed by the rumours about me,

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:52.390
you wouldn’t have forgotten what to do.

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:55.210
You can’t fight them just because I am gone?

00:13:55.210 --> 00:13:57.650
If so, you can’t possibly
protect the Earth.

00:13:58.260 --> 00:14:00.280
Are you really going to betray us?

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:03.860
Why don’t you answer?

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:06.900
If I was, what would you do?

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.660
Then I’d fight you, Oneesama!

00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:13.580
Mew Mew Mint METAMORPHO-SE!

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:28.380
Mew Mew Pomegranate METAMORPHO-SE!

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:00.160
I loved you!

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:01.710
I really loved you!

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:15.430
Shoot me, Minto!

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:16.680
Oneesama!

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:17.890
Stop!

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:20.520
Don’t do that, Minto!

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:23.650
Zakuro-san, you overdid it!

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:26.320
Get out of the way, Mew Strawberry!

00:15:26.810 --> 00:15:30.320
All the animals are trying desperately
to protect this planet!

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:36.040
Each of us has to do his best too, no matter
what the outcome turns out to be!

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:38.120
Even so, you are wrong!

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:40.960
<i>WE</i> are here to protect the Earth.

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:45.960
We must not fight each other,
no matter what reason we have!

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:50.970
What?

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:54.430
The birds are crying...

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:10.480
The birds are being sucked
into a twister!

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:15.890
A twister... in a place like this...?

00:16:15.890 --> 00:16:18.080
Everyone, be careful! That’s...

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:19.490
Heyhey!

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:20.290
Taru-taru!

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:22.620
How is it? Are you surprised?

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:27.420
All the birds in the bay are going
to die in the twister I generated.

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:31.010
Then all that will be left is to collect the Mew Aqua.

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:32.720
I won’t let you!

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:36.220
What’re you going to do?
Jump into the twister?

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:37.430
You’ll die!

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:40.310
Minto?

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:49.480
Where is it? Where?

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:52.820
What is she doing?

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:55.070
She wont be able to get out,
once she is sucked in.

00:16:55.070 --> 00:16:57.070
Minto, don’t go any further!

00:16:57.070 --> 00:16:58.370
Don’t worry!

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:00.790
I know my birds will answer me!

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:04.520
Leave everything to me! Answer me!

00:17:05.070 --> 00:17:08.620
I will protect the Earth and it’s nature, so <i>please</i>!

00:17:13.160 --> 00:17:15.340
Mew Strawberry, use the Mew Aqua Rod!

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:16.680
Ok!

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:19.890
The Mew Aqua responded?
Impossible!

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:21.180
Kuu Rai Sen!

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:25.280
MintonArrow!

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:31.110
Reborn... Mint... ECHO!

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:33.730
Minto!

00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:39.620
Mew Aqua Rod,

00:17:40.070 --> 00:17:41.830
SHINING!

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:48.130
Reborn Aqua Drops!

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:51.000
YAY!

00:18:54.770 --> 00:18:57.070
You did it! Amazing!

00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:58.400
Congratulations!

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:00.820
Both of you were so cool!

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:02.370
Ah don’t embarrass me...

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:04.080
I declare I lost.

00:19:05.980 --> 00:19:07.000
Zakuro-san.

00:19:08.030 --> 00:19:12.240
I often go to that church to visit
someone important to me...

00:19:12.240 --> 00:19:15.000
someone important who I’ve lost...

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:21.470
Confused by what others said, we doubted
each other even at the last moment.

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:24.980
Maybe that’s the reason I was so upset to see you guys making a fuss...

00:19:24.980 --> 00:19:27.020
...just because of some rumours.

00:19:28.780 --> 00:19:30.530
I’m sorry.

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:33.650
As Ichigo said, I overdid it.

00:19:34.070 --> 00:19:37.610
Zakuro-san, but why were you with Quiche?

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:42.070
Well... we were saying that the enemy
has feelings too, weren’t we?

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:44.620
I just thought it was a good opportunity to check it out.

00:19:45.260 --> 00:19:47.620
It seems they have a lot on their minds as well.

00:19:49.990 --> 00:19:51.080
Minto...?

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:52.960
What’s wrong, Minto?

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:55.300
No... nothing.

00:19:56.910 --> 00:19:57.750
Look...

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:01.760
Minto, I’m so sorry.

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:05.140
You’ve become so strong now...

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:07.470
...even I was impressed.

00:20:09.920 --> 00:20:10.890
Oneesama!

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:29.800
Wai! Wai! Bu-Ling has become the Queen of the Jungle!

00:20:30.430 --> 00:20:33.880
Bu-Ling, a huge area downtown has
turned into a forest overnight!

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:36.260
Now’s not the time to play around!

00:20:36.260 --> 00:20:40.880
Well, yeah, but still...
look at those nice huge trees!

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:46.470
Uwaah! Bu-Ling must play around
no matter who says what!

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:49.650
Next: “The City Turns into a Forest!
What Protects Ichigo’s Smile”

00:20:49.650 --> 00:20:54.070
Behave yourself, Bu-Ling! After all,
you’re here to fight for justice!
